  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 304 AM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nWith the ridge still overhead and only weak impulses passing well\nnorth of Kansas, clear and warm conditions are expected to continue.\nDaytime highs through the weekend are expected to reach the low to \nmid 80s for most of the area. Overnight lows remain in the 50s to \nnear 60 as efficient radiational cooling continues under clear sky \nand light wind.\n\nBy next week, long-range guidance shows a deep upper low developing \nover the western CONUS and eventually shifting east toward the \nPlains. This may be enough of a change in our weather pattern to \nbring at least some low chances of precipitation back to the area as\nearly as Tuesday. Temperatures should also be slightly cooler next\nweek with the breakdown of the ridge.",
